dialect protocol
protocol stdio.dxf.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.dxf
start body

# P2-FG1: `stdio.dxf` is TEXT-NATIVE (real R12 ASCII group-code/value pairs — there is no "binary
# DXF" at this standard; DXB is a wholly separate, unimplemented standard). The pack container IS
# the SEMIO envelope wrapping the artifact's own R12 ASCII text bytes verbatim
# (`ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with` in ../🦀️.rs: `print_dxf_document(self).into_bytes()`
# passed straight to `store::semio_format::wrap_binary` — no `pack_rt::encode_document` structured
# record, because `DxfSnapshot` has no derivable `RecordSpec`: `DxfEntity`/`DxfValue` are
# data-carrying enums with no `DslField` impl, same root cause `stdio.json`'s own `JsonValue`
# blocks `#[derive(dsl::DslArtifact)]` on).
#
# The framework-level SEMIO envelope itself (magic `0x8953454D0D0A1A0A` + LE u32 token length +
# UTF-8 token) is described ONCE, at
# `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio`
# (P2-M3 deliverable 3) — this file does NOT re-describe that framing. Cross-artifact
# `use semio.envelope` is not yet functional at `walk_protocol` time (confirmed unchanged through
# every pilot — json/csv/zip/png/txt/binary all independently re-confirmed this by direct read),
# so the envelope is deliberately NOT re-inlined here either: this file models the bytes as if the
# walk already starts AT the payload, past the envelope — the same honest boundary
# `m5_handcrafted_protocol_conformance`'s own `inner_payload_from_semio_example` exercises (it
# `unwrap_binary`s the fixture before handing bytes to `walk_protocol`), and the literal shape this
# artifact's own `protocol_walk_law` feeds `walk_protocol`.
#
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY layer by construction — its
# real internal shape (the group-code/value line-pair grammar, section/table/block/entity nesting)
# is `../📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio`'s job, not the protocol dialect's; DXF's tag-stream
# nesting has no fixed byte width to declare here. `chain payload utf8` is the same honest boundary
# `stdio.json`'s own snapshot protocol gives its opaque RFC8259 payload.
framing record
chain payload utf8
